---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';

const site = 'https://poke-survivors.org';
const title = 'Arceus Judgment Mode: Survive Past Minute 30 | PokéSurvivor';
const description = 'Master the Arceus Judgment Mode in PokéSurvivor. Learn how to survive past minute 30, unlock achievements, and climb the leaderboard in this endless challenge.';
const updated = '2026-10-19';
const gameVersion = '2026-10-13 update';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Can I skip the Judgment of Arceus?',
    a: 'No. The Judgment triggers automatically at minute 30. There is no way to avoid it—prepare for it instead.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you defeat Arceus?',
    a: 'No. Arceus is invincible in Judgment mode. The goal is survival time, not defeating it. (The "Defeat Arceus" achievement is from rift battles, a different mode—see our <a href="/rifts/">rifts guide</a>.)',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I lose my progress if I die in Judgment mode?',
    a: 'You keep all PokéCoins and gacha tickets earned before minute 30. Only the leaderboard survival time resets.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the world record survival time?',
    a: 'The leaderboard reset on October 13, 2026. Check <a href="https://pokesurvivor.com/en/" rel="noopener">pokesurvivor.com</a> for current records—they change daily.',
  },
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: title,
    description,
    datePublished: '2026-10-19',
    dateModified: updated,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PokeSurvivor Fan Guide' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PokeSurvivor Fan Guide' },
    inLanguage: 'en',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  alternates={[
    { locale: 'en', href: '/arceus-judgment/' },
    { locale: 'zh-Hant', href: '/zh/arceus-judgment/' }
  ]}
  description={description}
  keywords="arceus judgment mode, pokesurvivor 30 minutes, survive arceus, ruins of judgment, endless mode, pokesurvivor leaderboard, arceus achievements"
  ogType="article"
  ogImage="/og-arceus-judgment.jpg"
  ogImageAlt="Arceus Judgment Mode guide for PokéSurvivor"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Arceus Judgment', url: '/arceus-judgment/' }
  ]}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="page-wrapper">
    <article class="main-content">
      <header class="article-header">
        <p class="section-label">Guide</p>
        <h1>Arceus Judgment Mode: Survive Past Minute 30</h1>
        <p class="article-meta">
          Updated {updated} · Based on {gameVersion}
        </p>
      </header>


      <section>
        <h2>What is Arceus Judgment Mode?</h2>
        <p>
          You hit minute 30. The screen flashes. Arceus descends from the sky and drags you to the Ruins of Judgment.
          Your 29 minutes of grinding? Just the warmup.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Judgment of Arceus is PokéSurvivor's true endgame, introduced in the October 12-13 update that made runs
          endless. Before this, minute 30 was a victory screen. Now it's when the real fight starts.
        </p>
        <p>
          Arceus is invincible. It chases you, faster and faster. Every 5 seconds a legendary Pokémon joins the fight,
          each one with twice the HP and damage of the last. You can't beat this mode—you outlast it. The
          <a href="https://pokesurvivor.com/en/" rel="noopener">leaderboard</a> ranks survival time. How long can you last?
        </p>
        <p>
          New music plays. The atmosphere shifts. If you made it this far, you know the basics—check our
          <a href="/how-to-play/">how to play guide</a> if not. This guide is about surviving the Judgment.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The Judgment Mechanics</h2>

        <h3>Arceus is Invincible</h3>
        <p>
          You can't defeat Arceus. No health bar. No weakening phase. The moment you enter the Ruins of Judgment,
          your goal changes from offense to pure survival.
        </p>

        <figure class="content-image">
          <img
            src="/images/content/arceus-stat-comparison.svg"
            alt="Arceus base stat total compared to other legendary Pokémon like Mewtwo and Rayquaza"
            width="800"
            height="450"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>Arceus has the highest base stat total among all Pokémon—an unbeatable opponent</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Arceus chases you across the arena, and its speed ramps up over time. The official announcement says
          "faster and faster"—no public formula, but players report the pressure spikes noticeably after the first minute.
        </p>

        <h3>Legendary Pokémon Join Every 5 Seconds</h3>
        <p>
          The first legendary appears with boosted stats. Five seconds later, another joins with twice the HP and damage.
          Five seconds after that, a third with double the second's stats. The pattern continues.
        </p>
        <p>
          Here's what you face in the first minute:
        </p>
        <div class="data-table">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Time</th>
                <th>Legendaries on field</th>
                <th>Latest one's multiplier</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>0 sec</td><td>1</td><td>1×</td></tr>
              <tr><td>5 sec</td><td>2</td><td>2×</td></tr>
              <tr><td>10 sec</td><td>3</td><td>4×</td></tr>
              <tr><td>15 sec</td><td>4</td><td>8×</td></tr>
              <tr><td>30 sec</td><td>7</td><td>64×</td></tr>
              <tr><td>60 sec</td><td>13</td><td>4,096×</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          By the one-minute mark, 13 legendaries on screen, and the newest one hits four thousand times harder
          than the first. The difficulty curve isn't linear—it's exponential.
        </p>

        <figure class="content-image">
          <img
            src="/images/content/arceus-attack-timeline.svg"
            alt="Arceus attack pattern timeline showing three phases over 30 seconds"
            width="800"
            height="400"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>Attack phases repeat every 30 seconds—learn the pattern to survive longer</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h3>Surviving is the Only Goal</h3>
        <p>
          The October 13 update reset the all-time leaderboard. Everyone starts fresh. Your rank is your survival
          time: minute 31 is decent, minute 32 is strong, minute 33 puts you among the best.
        </p>
        <p>
          Solo and Group leaderboards are separate. Top spot? You're competing against every player worldwide,
          and the meta is still forming—this mode is only days old.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Survival Strategies</h2>

        <figure class="content-image">
          <img
            src="/images/content/judgment-arena-layout.svg"
            alt="Arceus Judgment arena showing safe zones and danger zones with attack patterns"
            width="800"
            height="450"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>Arena layout: Stay in the green safe zone and keep moving to avoid danger zones</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h3>Movement is Everything</h3>
        <p>
          Stop moving and you die. The 30 minutes before Judgment taught you to dodge hordes—Judgment demands you perfect it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Run wide circles or figure-eights. Tight loops let enemies surround you. Hug walls or corners, and Arceus
          plus the legendaries will box you in. Stay in open space, keep escape routes clear.
        </p>
        <p>
          PC: WASD or arrow keys. Mobile: the October 14 update added a responsive joystick—use it for precise
          dodging. Don't stand still to deal damage. Your partner attacks automatically; your job is staying alive.
        </p>

        <h3>Partner and Move Selection</h3>
        <p>
          Damage matters less than you think. A legendary with 4,096× HP won't go down quickly no matter what you're
          running. Prioritize survival stats:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Speed</strong> — outrun Arceus, reposition constantly.</li>
          <li><strong>HP and Defense</strong> — one mistake shouldn't end your run.</li>
          <li><strong>Sustain</strong> — healing moves or shields buy you seconds. Seconds add up.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Check our <a href="/tier-list/">partner tier list</a> and <a href="/best-pokemon/">best starter picks</a> for
          rankings. Early community testing says mobility-focused partners outperform glass cannons here, but the
          Judgment meta is still evolving.
        </p>
        <p>
          For moves: at least two damage options, fill the rest with utility—healing, shields, movement buffs.
          The Repertoire upgrade (start with 2 moves) is valuable. Get it for your main partner.
        </p>

        <h3>Use Your Upgrades Wisely</h3>
        <p>
          You level up during the first 30 minutes. The choices you make then decide whether you hit minute 31 or 33.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before minute 25, play for damage—farm XP efficiently. After minute 25, shift priorities:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Speed upgrades over damage upgrades</li>
          <li>HP and defense over offense</li>
          <li>Utility moves (heal, shield, dash) over raw DPS</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The 25-to-30 window is your prep phase. Make sure your move loadout and stat distribution are tuned for
          survival, not killing.
        </p>

        <h3>Don't Get Greedy</h3>
        <p>
          XP orbs drop from defeated enemies. Normally you chase them. In Judgment mode, chasing orbs gets you killed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Let orbs come to you. If one's on the other side of a legendary swarm, leave it. You don't need more
          levels—you need to not die. Same goes for trying to "clear" legendaries: you won't. Spawn rate's too high.
          This is a war of attrition. Focus on dodging, not fighting.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The Three Achievements</h2>
        <p>
          The October 13 update added three Judgment achievements. They're among the hardest in the game.
        </p>

        <div class="achievement-card">
          <h3>⭐ The Judgment</h3>
          <p class="achievement-unlock"><strong>Unlock:</strong> Reach the Judgment of Arceus (minute 30)</p>
          <p class="achievement-reward"><strong>Reward:</strong> Title <em>"Judged"</em></p>
          <p class="achievement-strategy">
            <strong>Strategy:</strong> Play solid for 30 minutes. Bosses at minutes 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 21, 24, 27
            are your checkpoints. Legendary rifts open from 1:15—clear them for ×10 gacha tickets (see our
            <a href="/rifts/">rifts guide</a>). By minute 25, tune your moves and stats toward survival.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="achievement-card">
          <h3>⭐⭐ Before the Creator</h3>
          <p class="achievement-unlock"><strong>Unlock:</strong> Survive 1 minute against Arceus</p>
          <p class="achievement-reward"><strong>Reward:</strong> Title <em>"Chosen of Arceus"</em></p>
          <p class="achievement-strategy">
            <strong>Strategy:</strong> Hit minute 31 (real time). Enter Judgment with full HP—heal up before
            minute 30 if needed. The first 30 seconds are easiest: only 7 legendaries on field, Arceus hasn't
            hit full speed yet. Wide movement, no risky plays. After 30 seconds, pressure doubles. Stay calm, keep running.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="achievement-card">
          <h3>⭐⭐⭐ Divine Challenge</h3>
          <p class="achievement-unlock"><strong>Unlock:</strong> Defeat 3 legendaries against Arceus in a single run</p>
          <p class="achievement-reward"><strong>Reward:</strong> None (no title listed)</p>
          <p class="achievement-strategy">
            <strong>Strategy:</strong> Brutal. You need high burst damage to kill legendaries before multipliers
            spiral out of control. Focus fire on the first 2-3 that spawn (0-15 seconds in). They're the weakest. After
            that, multipliers make kills nearly impossible. Bring a damage-focused partner, stack offensive upgrades in
            the 25-30 window, pray. Early reports say this is harder than hitting minute 32.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="achievement-note">
          <strong>Note:</strong> The "Defeat Arceus" achievement is separate—it's from rift battles, where you fight
          Arceus in a type arena. Different mode. Check our <a href="/rifts/">legendary rifts guide</a> for details.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Tips from the Community</h2>

        <h3>When to Start Preparing</h3>
        <p>
          Minute 25 is the cutoff. Before that, play aggressive—farm XP, stack damage, clear rifts. After minute 25, every
          level-up card choice should ask: "Does this help me live longer?"
        </p>
        <p>
          Check your HP. Below 80%? Look for healing. Check your move slots. Got 4 damage moves and no
          utility? Reroll for a shield or dash. Minutes 25 to 30 aren't about farming—they're about tuning your build for what's ahead.
        </p>

        <h3>Co-op Considerations</h3>
        <p>
          Playing with friends? Judgment works differently. Our <a href="/co-op/">co-op guide</a> covers multiplayer basics.
          Here are Judgment-specific notes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Revives</strong> — downed players can be revived by standing next to them for 3 seconds. In Judgment
            mode, 3 seconds is forever. Coordinate who goes for the revive—don't all clump together.</li>
          <li><strong>Spread out or stick together?</strong> — early testing is split. Spreading out splits enemy aggro but makes
            revives harder. Sticking together focuses fire but risks everyone dying at once. Experiment, see what works.</li>
          <li><strong>Voice chat</strong> — if your team has it, use it. Calling out Arceus position and legendary spawns
            saves lives.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Common Mistakes to Avoid</h3>
        <p>
          Mistakes I made, mistakes I see in streams:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Entering Judgment below 50% HP</strong> — heal up before minute 30. One early hit shouldn't end your run.</li>
          <li><strong>Standing in corners</strong> — corners feel safe. They're death traps. Arceus and legendaries will
            pin you. Stay in open ground.</li>
          <li><strong>Chasing kills</strong> — you won't clear the board. Stop trying. Your goal is time, not kills.</li>
          <li><strong>Tunnel vision on one legendary</strong> — while you focus-fire one, three more spawn behind you. Keep
            your awareness wide.</li>
          <li><strong>Ignoring the October 8 enemy types</strong> — the update added healers, shielders, summoners, exploders.
            They show up in Judgment too. Prioritize exploders (the glowing ones)—they can one-shot you if you're not careful.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How the Leaderboard Works</h2>
        <p>
          The all-time leaderboard reset on October 13, 2026. Everyone's at zero. Your rank is your best survival time:
          how many seconds past minute 0 you lasted.
        </p>
        <p>
          Solo and Group leaderboards are separate, so you can chase both. The leaderboard is global—you're competing
          against every PokéSurvivor player, not just your region.
        </p>
        <p>
          No official world record yet (the mode's 6 days old as of this writing), but community Discord
          channels are tracking 32+ minute runs. That number will climb. Check
          <a href="https://pokesurvivor.com/en/" rel="noopener">pokesurvivor.com</a> for live standings.
        </p>
        <p>
          One minute past Judgment (minute 31) puts you ahead of most players. Two minutes (minute 32)? Elite territory.
          Three minutes? You're in the conversation for top-tier runs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <FAQ heading="Common Questions" items={faq} />

      <aside class="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title">
        <h2 id="sources-title">Sources and Updates</h2>
        <p>
          This guide is based on the <a href="https://pokesurvivor.com/en/news/" rel="noopener">official October 13, 2026
          update announcement</a>, the <a href="https://pokesurvivor.com/en/achievements/" rel="noopener">achievements page</a>,
          and community play experience. We are fans who play PokéSurvivor, not the developers.
        </p>
        <p>
          Game mechanics may change in future updates. If any numbers on this page conflict with the game, trust the game.
          Always check <a href="https://pokesurvivor.com/en/" rel="noopener">pokesurvivor.com</a> for the latest information.
        </p>
        <p class="version-info">
          <strong>Game version:</strong> October 13, 2026 update<br>
          <strong>Guide last updated:</strong> October 19, 2026
        </p>
      </aside>
    </article>

    <section class="closing-cta" aria-labelledby="closing-cta-title">
      <h2 id="closing-cta-title">Ready to Face Arceus?</h2>
      <p>The Judgment waits at minute 30. How long will you last?</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="https://pokesurvivor.com/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Play PokéSurvivor</a>
        <a href="/how-to-play/" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">Learn the Basics</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-wrapper {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .main-content {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-2xl) var(--container-padding);
  }

  .article-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .section-label {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    background: var(--accent-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--font-semibold);
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .article-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(var(--font-size-3xl), 5vw, var(--font-size-4xl));
    font-weight: var(--font-bold);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .article-meta {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .version-alert {
    background: var(--surface-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .version-alert a {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

